    {
     "q": "What does FAT prove if the skid runs on your test water, not our feed?",
     "a": "Function: every sequence, alarm, interlock and divert, a sanitization cycle reaching temperature at every probe, instrument loop checks, and outlet quality on our test water. Performance on your feed water is proven at SAT and OQ. We write the protocol so your quality unit can leverage FAT results under Annex 15, 3.6 and ASTM E2500, where it accepts that approach."
    },
    {
     "q": "Will our quality unit accept FAT results in place of IQ/OQ tests?",
     "a": "That is its decision, and Annex 15 sets the test: appropriate, justified and unaffected by transport and installation. It helps when the leverage is planned, not argued afterwards. We mark candidate test cases in the commissioning and qualification plan at detailed design, your quality unit approves the FAT protocol before execution (Annex 15, 2.6), and the report shows calibrated instruments, raw data and signatures. Water quality on your feed and anything touching site utilities is never leveraged."
    },
    {
     "q": "Can we use our own protocol template?",
     "a": "Yes. We write into your template and numbering, or deliver ours for you to adopt. Either way each test case carries a URS or functional specification reference, so it lands in your traceability matrix."
    },
    {
     "q": "What can a remote witness not see?",
     "a": "Smell, noise and heat, the inside of a panel unless the camera is opened up to it, and the thread engagement of a fitting. For a remote FAT we agree in the protocol which checks need a person on site, and either send you close-up video and photos with the record or recommend a hybrid witness for those tests."
    },
    {
     "q": "What if a test fails while you are watching?",
     "a": "It is recorded as found, as a deviation. We do not edit the acceptance criterion or quietly rerun the test; Annex 15, 2.7 treats a significant change to the approved protocol as a deviation too. We investigate, fix, and retest that case and any case the fix could affect, with you witnessing the retest."
    },
    {
     "q": "Is the software we see at FAT the software that ships?",
